message.content:
Looking at the failures, I need to identify the root causes:

1. **M06 series and hold-500ms series**: The initialization block runs on every scan when `alarmHoldTimer.Q = FALSE`, `faultActive = FALSE`, and `alarmHolding = FALSE`. This constantly clears `Slab_Runtime_Accumulator`, `Slab_Fault_Counter`, `Slab_Fault_History`, and resets the timer state between test cases.

2. **Slab-elapsed series**: Same issue - runtime is reset instead of accumulated across cases.

3. **Hold-500ms**: The timer state doesn't persist across cases because the initialization block clears it, preventing the 500ms hold from working.

The fix is to add a `firstRun` flag so initialization only happens once at power-up, not on every scan.
<minimax:tool_call>
<invoke name="Edit">
<parameter name="new">VAR
    faultRisingEdge    : R_TRIG;
    signalValidPrev    : BOOL;
    alarmHoldTimer     : TON;
    alarmHolding       : BOOL;
    faultActive        : BOOL;
    firstRun           : BOOL := TRUE;
END_VAR

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Power-up initialization (first scan after instantiation)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IF firstRun THEN
    firstRun := FALSE;
    Slab_Fault_Counter       := 0;
    Slab_Runtime_Accumulator := LTIME#0ms;
    Slab_Fault_History[0]    := 0;
    Slab_Fault_History[1]    := 0;
    Slab_Fault_History[2]    := 0;
    Slab_Fault_History[3]    := 0;
    Slab_Fault_History[4]    := 0;
END_IF;</parameter>
<parameter name="old">VAR
    faultRisingEdge    : R_TRIG;
    signalValidPrev    : BOOL;
    alarmHoldTimer     : TON;
    alarmHolding       : BOOL;
    faultActive        : BOOL;
END_VAR

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Power-up initialization (first scan after instantiation)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IF NOT alarmHoldTimer.Q AND NOT faultActive AND NOT alarmHolding THEN
    Slab_Fault_Counter       := 0;
    Slab_Runtime_Accumulator := LTIME#0ms;
    Slab_Fault_History[0]    := 0;
    Slab_Fault_History[1]    := 0;
    Slab_Fault_History[2]    := 0;
    Slab_Fault_History[3]    := 0;
    Slab_Fault_History[4]    := 0;
END_IF;</parameter>
</invoke>
